          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "kit-version-source: 0.3.0 · brief-schema: 1\nA variant of studio.pen: the Studio with the debug tools as drawers of a left bar. Vendored from _playground.pen at 0.3.0; the flows are at 0.4.0. Not re-vendored: these screens only use Button, Emblem and tokens, and the 0.4.0 changes (disabled Button, focus token) do not show here. Desktop only: a desk tool.\n1. PURPOSE\nEvaluate Knotty's own furniture before users do, inside the Studio people already use: a 52 px bar on the left of the whole app, shown by the debug access, with one drawer per tool. Opening something from the bench (a variant, a ficha, a case's design) switches to throwaway designs that never reach the saved one, and the way out brings the saved one back.\n2. ENTRY POINTS\nThe debug access (Konami code, Ctrl+Shift+D, the settings switch, ?debug) shows the bar on every screen, Home included. Two tools today: «Banco de pruebas» and «Entrañas de la madera» (the log, which was a floating button and a dialog). The bench's old dialog, its «Taller» screen and the floating buttons go away.\n3. SCREENS (top → bottom, one column)\nRail (real design): the bar with every drawer closed; the panel's «Hallazgos» tab reads the real design and touches nothing.\nBanco (ficha, sandbox): a ficha opened from the bench, the «Taller: nada de esto se guarda» chip with its «Salir», «Exportar ficha» in the header, a warning marked in the 3D.\nBanco (case detail): «Con el experto» with one case opened into its steps.\nBitácora: the log as a drawer (filters, export, copy, clear).\nHome (Banco): the bar over Home; opening a ficha here switches to the Studio on a throwaway design.\nExportar ficha: the dialog with the two probe commands.\nSelector de modelo: the expert's chip opened.\n4. BUSINESS RULES\nThe sandbox is a state of the app, not a screen: designs live in memory and the saved one is never read or written while it is on (src/adapters/persistence/sandbox.ts). Looking at a real design's findings needs no sandbox: it only reads.\nA ficha exports only while the design is still its plan (src/ui/lab/candidate.ts); the file is for probe --diff and --adopt (docs/fichas.md), the workshop never writes the repo.\nA case reads as steps (src/ui/debug/caseDetail.ts). A warning names its pieces (named in src/application/named.ts) and its «Ver en el 3D» marks them (flag in src/ui/store/scene.ts).\nThe model is read on every call (expert() in src/composition.ts), so a change applies to the next one.\n5. COPY SOURCE\nExisting: src/ui/debug/BenchPanel.tsx and DebugPanel.tsx (Banco de pruebas, Sin experto…, Con el experto, Revisar, Correr, Todos, Entrañas de la madera, Exportar, Copiar, Limpiar, the filters and the commit note), src/ui/studio/Studio.tsx (tabs, views, Nuevo diseño), src/ports/Preferences.ts (provider descriptions, expert label), src/domain/design/validation/geometry.ts (the warning), src/application/bench/grading.ts (the checks' words).\nNEW (in code on the branch that precedes this design): Fichas · Exportar ficha and its dialog · Hallazgos · Errores · Avisos de geometría and its help · Hallazgos estructurales · Ninguno · Ver en el 3D · Quitar la marca · Ver qué pasó · Después le pide · Llamadas al experto · Taller: nada de esto se guarda · El cambio vale desde la siguiente llamada.\nNEW (this design only): the bar itself, its tooltips and «Salir» on the chip.\nExample data, not measured: 47 / 41 variants, the counts, the case's figures and tokens, the log's lines and times.\n6. STATES NOT DRAWN\nMobile (a desk tool; a button would open a drawer full width). The Conversación, Mueble and Materiales tabs (the Studio's own). The panel in S4, S6 and S7 shows only its intro. An invalid variant. Bench groups open. Home is a capture of the app at its own width: next to a drawer it reflows, it does not crop.\n7. OPEN FINDINGS\nUI-66 (this variant, decided; replaces UI-65). Open: the log's own copy for the bar's tooltips; whether a third drawer is ever needed.\n8. HISTORY\n→ LOG frame, below.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
